  "x-semantic-checks": [
    "DC01: n equals len(entity_ids)>=2; K equals len(criterion_ids)>=1; all IDs are opaque nonblank strings and retain declared order. targets contains exactly one record per criterion ID.",
    "DC02: every numeric cell is finite, complete, and already on the declared orientation; no R NA/NaN/Inf, no JSON extensions, no coercion, filling, jitter, sorting, or implicit axis inference.",
    "DC03: joint tensor values and dimnames have exactly S x n x K shape with named axes draw/entity/criterion. Each criterion matrix has its own S_k x n shape, S_k>=1. Singleton dimensions remain present.",
    "DC04: each matrix/tensor entity axis equals the global ordered entity_ids; joint criterion axis equals criterion_ids. Criterion blocks cover global criterion_ids exactly once; unequal S_k and sampler regimes are allowed without cross-block row alignment.",
    "DC05: draw_index covers local draw slots exactly once. original_draw_id is unique within each source fit input. For MCMC each retained (chain_id,iteration) is unique and the original_draw_id map is one-to-one. IID chain_id and iteration are null; source draw IDs are retained.",
    "DC06: MCMC chain histories cover the declared chain IDs exactly once. Retained, warmup and discarded iterations are disjoint; each list preserves original chronology; retained coordinates exactly match draw_index; no unknown warmup history substituted by an empty list.",
    "DC07: joint-mode row vectors preserve all entity x criterion targets from the same genuine posterior draw. Criterionwise rows preserve all entities within that criterion. Provenance is declared, not inferable from equal row counts or matching keys.",
    "DC08: variable_map covers entity x criterion exactly once (joint) or entity x its block criterion exactly once. Source target-variable IDs are unique within an origin; derived targets require explicit derivation_note and precomputation from intact original draws, not marginal shuffling.",
    "DC09: repeated source_id / fit_id / model_id declarations across blocks are consistent. Repeated original draw IDs across criteria are permitted only with consistent original identity, but do not by themselves establish cross-criterion coupling.",
    "DC10: targets are scientifically comparable across entities; identification, orientation, transformation, units and conditioning are explicit. A validator checks declarations and cannot verify posterior correctness or solve unidentified labels/factor sign/rotation.",
    "DC11: any within-criterion entity tie in a retained draw or positive-mass finite state triggers rejection/review for this version. No observed ties does not prove a tie-free law; continuous univariate marginals alone do not rule out joint degeneracy.",
    "DC12: finite-law state IDs are unique; every theta is n x K safe integers; all state numerators positive and their exact sum equals denominator without exceeding safe integer bounds. This is an explicitly defined exact law, not an empirical or weighted approximation renamed as exact.",
    "DC13: requested functionality is expected_rank_loss only. No joint-tail, chance-risk or simultaneous-error certificate is implemented, even for a genuine joint tensor.",
    "DC14: weighted importance/SMC, variational, unknown sampling regimes and unknown target distribution are outside this version. Weights must not be dropped, equalized, or rebranded as exact finite mass. Equal-weight variational/approximate-posterior draws are also unsupported here.",
    "DC15: source artifact hashes and mapping assertions are provenance records. Actual source-value equality is checked only if a future adapter reads the source. Output must distinguish schema_checked, semantic_checks_completed, source_values_checked, jointness_verified=false and convergence_verified=false."
  ]
}
